# Entries `nr-tools libc-interpose` refuses for glibc 2.39-0ubuntu8.12, and why.
#
# `nr-tools libc-patch` asserts **set equality** against this list, so:
#   * a refusal that is not listed here fails the build (the transform silently
#     lost coverage - the bug this assertion exists for);
#   * a listed entry that starts being patched also fails (glibc changed or the
#     interposer was improved) - review, then drop the line.
# Do not add a line to silence a failure without knowing the reason.
# The first four are 24-byte fortify wrappers: the only branch "into the
# window" is their own `b.hi`/`tbl` to +0xc, and their real path is a tail
# branch to readlink / readlinkat / realpath / mq_open - all four are patched
# entries in the table, so covering the wrapper would add nothing. Verified by
# disassembly in evidence 175.
__readlink_chk         # self-branch to +0xc; tail-calls patched readlink
__readlinkat_chk       # self-branch to +0xc; tail-calls patched readlinkat
__realpath_chk         # self-branch to +0xc; tail-calls patched realpath
__mq_open_2            # tbnz to +0x8; tail-calls patched mq_open
# This one is UNKNOWN, not verified: not exported by this libc build, so the
# slot page cannot even locate it. Its callers are libc-internal and their outer
# entries are patched, but that is an argument, not a measurement (evidence 175).
__openat64_nocancel    # not exported by this libc (stripped .symtab)
